Atlas overlay patch 0071: ui/omnibox-find-ring
Why: the omnibox, load bar, find bar and downloads button of tokens.md section 4 and 8 (a download shows its ring and opens no popup unless clicked: the default of the partial-view pref is off, a one-line default because a first-run pref would not reach existing profiles; the list header is a section header: upper case, 11 px, dim; the omnibox centred in the toolbar and 560 px wide at most: the default of the centred-address-bar pref and its width constant): a 1 px `line` border on the idle omnibox, the focus ring 2 px outside the field, the load bar a solid 2 px `accent` line that follows the load value (the inherited bar has a glow and a pulse), the find bar 36 px high with its count at 11 px. The paint and the font helper are in chrome/browser/ui/atlas/chrome (overlay tree); the patch is the hook lines. No lower tier reaches view painting.
Files: chrome/browser/ui/browser_ui_prefs.cc, chrome/browser/ui/views/toolbar/toolbar_view.cc, chrome/browser/download/download_prefs.cc, chrome/browser/ui/views/download/bubble/download_dialog_view.cc, chrome/browser/ui/BUILD.gn, chrome/browser/ui/views/location_bar/location_bar_view.cc, chrome/browser/ui/views/location_bar/location_bar_progress_view.cc, chrome/browser/ui/views/find_bar_view.cc
Test filter: *AtlasTokens*; reel scenes R02 (omnibox, ring, load bar), R10 (find bar)
Rebase risk: M (the progress view is a file of the inherited series; one early-return hook before its glow code)
Release: 0.13
License: GPL-3.0-or-later (hunks in files the inherited series touches or adds)
Verified at: 156.0.8078.79, prepared tree with the inherited and platform series applied

